# Wonder Field
#
# What a wonder is, where new ones come from, and what lets one close.
# Read from two mounted consumers' November caches and from a count of this repo's own wonders (2026-11-09).
# The wonders at the end are written to be run: each names a command that works in this repo today.
#
# @see docs/theory/spw/threshold-distance.spw
# @see docs/theory/spw/exhibit-floor.spw
# @see .spw/harness/claim-protocol.spw
# @see .spw/caches/journal/2026-11-09-consumer-caches.spw

#>wonder_field
#:layer #!pragmatics
#:status #!seeded

^["contract"]{
 exploratory: "A theory notebook of readings, not runtime or parser law; a claim here binds only once a runtime or parser contract repeats it."
 owners: "A wonder filed by a consumer keeps its owner. This surface reads their wonders as examples and answers none of them."
 measured: "Counts are from the journal entry 2026-11-09-consumer-caches and are counts on that day."
}

^["roots"]{
 @journal: ~"../../../.spw/caches/journal/2026-11-09-consumer-caches.spw"
 @distance: ~"./threshold-distance.spw"
 @floor: ~"./exhibit-floor.spw"
 @protocol: ~"../../../.spw/harness/claim-protocol.spw"
 @inquiry: ~"../../../.agents/plans/inquiry-loop/wip.spw"
 @trials: ~"../../../.agents/plans/interpretation-trials/interpretation-trials.spw"
 @line_kit: ~"../../../.agents/plans/line-kit/wip.spw"
 @bench: ~"../../../scripts/analyzers/spw-trial-bench.ts"
}

^["thesis"]{
 ~#claim: "A wonder is a line one edit past what already reads. Its measures name the ways it could come out, its expect is a guess among them, and its probe is the act that tells."
 ~#claim: "A wonder closes on a receipt. A probe that is a prompt to think leaves none, so a field of such wonders grows and never settles."
 ~#law: "Write the expect before the probe runs. Keep the question's owner. Answer nothing in passing."
 ~#refuse: #[
  "a wonder that counts everything: it has no seat and no end",
  "a wonder generated from a template with no line it is one edit from",
  "an answer written where a retirement was meant: a question withdrawn was not resolved",
 ]
}

^["as_question"]{
 # The reading a consumer's cache gives, and what each field then is.
 resolutions: "a question denotes the set of answers that would settle it; $%[a, b, c] writes that set down"
 expect: "~#expect is a guess over the set, made before looking"
 answer: "~#answer picks a member of the set, with the receipt that picked it"
 retired: "~#retired withdraws the question; nothing is claimed about the set"
 open_on_purpose: "some questions are kept open because asking them is the practice: one host refuses to fold a question's body, and a second keeps one wonder that is never answered"
 consequence: "a wonder whose $% does not partition its outcomes cannot be answered cleanly; the measures are the first thing to check"
}

^["across_hosts"]{
 workbench: "an anchor, a ? frame, a depth, a hypothesis, a probe and measures; a harvest reads them"
 site_consumer: "the same frame with ~#with, ~#expect, ~#probe(run) or ~#probe(read), and a rule that a wonder names one seat, one probe and three outcomes"
 canvas: "a question's body opens from its middle and refuses the fold"
 story_site: "a wonder is veiled until met, glimpsed, then found; it closes when kept or answered; a question room is cast by answering it"
 shared: "every host gives the open question a rendering that does not resolve. None yet shows how far a question is from closing."
}

^["census"]{
 here: "747 wonder anchors outside archives; 58 with an expect; 22 with an answer written, 34 with the answer left as a hole; 1 retired"
 probes: "1,448 probe blocks, 2 of them marked to run"
 reading: "About one wonder in thirteen says what it expects, and about one in thirty-four has been answered. The field is wide and almost none of it can close, because almost no probe is a command."
 contrast: "The site consumer lists 383 wonders by script and marks each probe run or read. A second mounted consumer holds 81 wonders a reader can keep, and every one of them closes by being kept."
}

^["neighbors"]{
 # Where a good wonder comes from: one edit away from a line that already reads.
 pivot: "change one slot, turn one mark, add or drop one part: the lines one change away are a line's neighbors, and each is a question about what the change says"
 hole: "replace one word with _: the shape that remains asks what else fills it"
 parting: "run two readers over one form: where they part is a question neither reader asked"
 edge: "a surface the index does not reach asks whether it is arriving or leaving"
 host: "the same line on two hosts: where the renderings differ is a question about the mark or about the host"
 rule: "A wonder made this way has a seat (the edit), an end (the edit reads or it does not), and three outcomes at most: both readers take it, one does, neither does."
 not_this: "The product of every mark, container, slot, clock and material is almost all uninhabited. Walking it by template gives questions nobody was near enough to ask."
}

^["grain"]{
 consumer_rule: "a plan is one wonder wide until a probe shows two places must change together"
 here: "48 live plans hold 195 open questions; 2 plans are one wonder wide"
 reading: "Most open questions here sit inside plans that also carry seven planned commits. A question inside a wide plan waits on the plan; a question that is the plan waits only on its probe."
 move: "Before a plan opens, write its wonder and run its probe. If the probe names one file, the wonder was the plan."
}

^["runnable"]{
 # Three kinds of probe, by what they leave behind.
 run: "a command that reads and prints; it leaves an observation with a date and an exit code"
 read: "named files and what to look for; it leaves a quote and a location"
 think: "a prompt; it leaves nothing a second reader can check"
 law: "A probe marked run must be read-only. A probe that would write is a plan, and says so."
 receipt: "the observation, the date, the command and the revision it ran against, kept beside the wonder and not in its question"
}

^["falsify"]{
 neighbors_are_dull: "If wonders made from pivots are answered at once and teach nothing, distance one is too near and the field needs two edits."
 census_misleads: "If most of the 1,448 prompts were read and acted on without a receipt, the field closes more than the count shows."
 grain_is_taste: "If one-wonder plans land no sooner than wide ones in this repo's own history, the consumer's rule is a preference."
}

#>wonder_docs_theory_spw_wonderfield_1
?["Where seed's two readers part on a trial form, is the form one edit from a form they agree on?"]{
 #:depth #!syntax ~#lens(comparison)
 ~#hypothesis: "Each parting on the gap and dot cards disappears when one separator is changed, so a parting is a neighbor of an agreement."
 ~#expect: "garden{seed.water} parts and garden{seed; water} does not; *wonders{ @a $b #c } parts and *wonders{ @a, $b, #c } does not."
 ~#probe(run)
 !probe{ "npm run -s analyze:trials -- --card gap" }
 $%[parting.one_edit_away, parting.further, parting.no_neighbor]
}

#>wonder_docs_theory_spw_wonderfield_2
?["Can a request be written as a line: the method a mark, the path a word, a query key a mode, the carried line a body, the representation a concept?"]{
 #:depth #!semantics ~#lens(projection)
 ~#hypothesis: "An address has five seats and a line has five slots, so a request reads as a line with no new grammar, and a route is a line a reader can say aloud."
 ~#expect: "The line reader reads ?guide/read[line]{garden}<text> whole; the parser reads the nested form as two expressions; a route with @ reads as a join."
 ~#probe(run)
 !probe{ "npm run -s analyze:trials -- --card address_line" }
 $%[request.reads_in_both, request.line_reader_only, request.neither]
}

#>wonder_docs_theory_spw_wonderfield_3
?["Can a line say when it ends?"]{
 #:depth #!semantics ~#lens(choice)
 ~#hypothesis: "An expiry is a concept or a scene on the line it ends, and the only thing missing is a date the parser reads."
 ~#expect: "The line reader reads <until 2026-11-26> as a concept; the parser reports errors on the date."
 ~#probe(run)
 !probe{ "npm run -s analyze:trials -- --card until" }
 $%[expiry.concept, expiry.scene, expiry.stance, expiry.unread]
}

#>wonder_docs_theory_spw_wonderfield_4
?["Does a query's output still carry the marks of the line it read?"]{
 #:depth #!computational ~#lens(projection)
 ~#hypothesis: "The JSON rows keep the mark and the brace as fields and the text as written, so a pipe loses the line's order and nesting and keeps its marks."
 ~#expect: "Each row has sigil, brace and text; no row holds a Spw frame a second plugin could parse without the file."
 ~#probe(run)
 !probe{ "npm run -s spw:query -- --from docs/theory/spw/wonder-field.spw --selector pathRefs --json" }
 $%[pipe.keeps_marks, pipe.keeps_frames, pipe.keeps_neither]
}

#>wonder_docs_theory_spw_wonderfield_5
?["Do plans with one open question land sooner than plans with five?"]{
 #:depth #!pragmatics ~#lens(comparison)
 ~#hypothesis: "A plan that is one wonder wide waits only on its probe, so landed plans skew toward few open questions when they opened."
 ~#expect: "The index shows open counts today, not at opening, so this needs each plan's first commit; the hypothesis may not be testable from the index alone."
 ~#probe(run)
 !probe{ "npm run -s spw:plan:index" }
 $%[grain.narrow_lands_sooner, grain.no_difference, grain.not_measurable]
}

#>wonder_docs_theory_spw_wonderfield_6
?["Could a wonder arrive veiled: its question shown only after its probe has been run once?"]{
 #:depth #!experiential ~#lens(choice)
 ~#hypothesis: "A reader who runs a probe before reading its question meets the observation without a guess to defend, and writes a truer expect for the next reader."
 ~#expect: "No tool here hides a question. A host that veils wonders until they are met already orders discovery this way for a reader who is not the author."
 !probe{ "give two readers the same three wonders, one with questions shown and one with only the probe commands; compare the expects they write afterwards" }
 $%[veil.truer_expect, veil.no_difference, veil.lost_readers]
}

#>wonder_docs_theory_spw_wonderfield_7
?["Which wonders are still worth a probe a year after they were written?"]{
 #:depth #!pragmatics ~#lens(comparison)
 ~#hypothesis: "A wonder lasts when it sits one edit from a line people still write, and fades when its line stopped being written."
 ~#expect: "Among wonders older than ninety days here, the ones still cited from a live plan name a form on a trial card."
 !probe{ "list wonder anchors with the date their file was first committed and the live plans that cite them; read the ten oldest still cited" }
 $%[lasting.near_a_live_line, lasting.cited_by_habit, lasting.none_survive]
}
